module

public import Theory.GroupTheory.Recognition.ReeTwo.SmallParityRepresentatives
import Mathlib.Tactic.FinCases

/-!
# Nodes for the Ree two parity census

This fixed family is intended for maximal-subgroup descent outside the parity
kernel. The top entry is explicit, and the nineteen proposed survivors are
identified with their existing public representatives. The other entries are
subgroups generated by the displayed root words. This module asserts neither
exhaustiveness nor the orders or Frattini properties of the other entries.

The diagnostic labels match the full exploratory centric census; the `Fin 131`
indices retain just the entries outside parity. Labels are only lookup aids.
The two leading binary root letters are combined into powers of `rootOne`.

Source: Shinoda (1975), (2.3), pp.81–82, in the verified root model of
`ReeTwo.Sylow`; root words from the saved centric enumeration. External
calculations select the definitions but supply no proof of coverage.
-/

namespace ReeTwo.SylowModel

